From d7d3dcd3c7b80001c1fbb6e9d342ac30df90d39c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wwoosshh <s01055310644@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:06:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [inductor] Guard reinplacing into an overwritten input
 for multi-output ops and chains

Extend the check to every value that would share the input's buffer once
the node is reinplaced: the node's views and getitem outputs (so
auto_functionalized / triton / foreach nodes are covered), and the
results of later ops that may be reinplaced into one of those. If the
copy_ epilogue writes back one of these values, it writes back the
node's own result; any other value overwrites the buffer, and then none
of them may be used after that copy_. This fixes

    boo(x); y = x.clone(); x.fill_(2.0); return y   # custom op
    y = x.index_put(...); w = y.index_put(...); x.zero_(); return w

which still returned the overwritten values.

Split the test into parametrized cases, add the two above, and check
that the patterns whose write-back is the result itself still reinplace
(num_reinplacing_failures() == 0).
---
 test/inductor/test_inplacing_pass.py   | 126 ++++++++++++++++++++-----
 torch/_inductor/fx_passes/reinplace.py |  58 ++++++++----
 2 files changed, 141 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

